# =============================================================================
# dropbear-initramfs Configuration Template
# =============================================================================
#
# This file configures the Dropbear SSH server used within the initramfs
# environment. It is sourced by the initramfs scripts during early boot,
# allowing remote SSH access to unlock disks or troubleshoot boot issues.
#
# IMPORTANT: Changes to this file require running `update-initramfs -u`
# to rebuild the initial ramdisk image for the changes to take effect.
#
# Variable assignment follows shell semantics. String values must be
# quoted if they contain spaces or special characters.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Command line options to pass to dropbear(8)
#
# This variable allows passing additional arguments to the dropbear binary.
# Common options include -p (port), -r (host key), or -I (banner file).
# See dropbear(8) for available options.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Schema Default: ''
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DROPBEAR_OPTIONS="{{ DROPBEAR_OPTIONS | default('') }}"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Network interface pattern to bring down after initramfs.
#
# This variable specifies a glob pattern for network interfaces that should
# be brought down when exiting the initramfs environment (on local/non-NFS
# mounts). This prevents dirty network configuration from persisting into
# the normal root filesystem environment.
#
# Special Value: 'none'
#   If set to 'none', all interfaces are kept up. This preserves routing
#   tables and addresses, which may be desirable if the network configuration
#   was established correctly in initramfs and should be inherited by the
#   main system.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Schema Default: '*'
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
IFDOWN="{{ IFDOWN | default('*') }}"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maximum seconds to wait for network/dropbear setup at init-bottom.
#
# On local (non-NFS) mounts, the network stack and dropbear are started
# asynchronously during the init-premount stage. This timeout specifies the
# maximum number of seconds to wait at the init-bottom stage before
# terminating dropbear and bringing the network down.
#
# If this timeout is too short, and the boot process is not blocking on
# user input via SSH (e.g., no remote LUKS unlocking is required), the
# initrd might pivot to the real root (init(1)) too early. This can cause
# a race condition between the network configuration established in
# initramfs and the network configuration applied by the normal system.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Schema Default: 60
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DROPBEAR_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT={{ DROPBEAR_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT | default(60) }}